     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><br><br>On Thursday, November 14, 2013 at 11:42:59 PM UTC-8, Hjyah wrote:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\">Hello,</span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\">Thank you very much to your\r\nteam effort for a great development and service because Shiny and RStudio are\r\nvery helpful in moving local R scripts to the web!</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\">I posted this question on\r\nStackOverflow, <span style=\"color:rgb(34,34,34)\"><a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/19988160/oauth-from-httr-to-linkedin-on-a-shiny-server\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/19988160/oauth-from-httr-to-linkedin-on-a-shiny-server&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792392296516000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1J5Fwuw1kAl5pXYAoPNL5b\">OAuth (from“httr”) to LinkedIn on a Shiny server</a></span>, and here because of the use\r\nof multiple packages.  </span></p>\r\n\r\n<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\">I apologize for cross posting the question between different sites because\r\nI thought that I may receive a Shiny answer if I posted here. If there is a\r\nsolution, feel free to share it as an answer on <a href=\"http://stackoverflow.com/questions/19988160/oauth-from-httr-to-linkedin-on-a-shiny-server\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://stackoverflow.com/questions/19988160/oauth-from-httr-to-linkedin-on-a-shiny-server&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792392296516000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1J5Fwuw1kAl5pXYAoPNL5b\">SO</a>\r\nas well.</span><div><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:115%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-position:initial initial;background-repeat:initial initial\"><br></span></div><div><p style=\"font-size:14px;clear:both;color:rgb(0,0,0);font-family:Arial,&#39;Liberation Sans&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans&#39;,sans-serif\">I’m trying to connect to the LinkedIn API using OAuth from the &#39;httr&#39; library on a &#39;Shiny&#39; server. I have wrapped the locally working OAuth example from <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/httr/blob/master/demo/oauth1-linkedin.r\" rel=\"nofollow\" style=\"background-color:transparent;color:rgb(74,107,130)\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/httr/blob/master/demo/oauth1-linkedin.r&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792392296516000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2Whg7JjsUuG0EvZkKIKAWo\">GitHub/hadley/httr</a>, with a Shiny client ui and server side. I get the client ui working.</p><pre style=\"margin-bottom:10px;padding:5px;font-size:14px;background-color:rgb(238,238,238);font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,serif;overflow:auto;width:auto;max-height:600px;word-wrap:normal;color:rgb(0,0,0);line-height:18px\"><code style=\"font-family:Consolas,Menlo,Monaco,&#39;Lucida Console&#39;,&#39;Liberation Mono&#39;,&#39;DejaVu Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Bitstream Vera Sans Mono&#39;,&#39;Courier New&#39;,monospace,serif\"><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">library</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">(</span><span style=\"background-color:transparent\">shiny</span><span style=\"background-c